{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [56.9763, 40.578072399999996, 166.85698432000004, 52.57797239999991], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "MAJOR ARTICLE"}, {"bbox": [348.3333333333333, 6.666666666666629, 491.0, 60.66666666666663], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "OIDSA"}, {"bbox": [48.9826, 86.10906509999995, 513.1769895400001, 152.8774239077028], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "Efficacy and Safety of Doravirine-based Regimens by Sex and Race: Long-term Results From Three Phase 3 Clinical Trials"}, {"bbox": [48.9826, 158.33826999999997, 533.2808668, 177.95597239999995], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "Sharon L. Walmsley, 1, Princy N. Kumar, 2 Chloe Orkin, 3, Melanie Thompson, 4 Kathleen Squires, 5,† Zhi Jin Xu, 5 Wayne Greaves, 5 Rebeca M. Plank, 5, Yohance Whiteside, 5 and Rima Lahoulou 6"}, {"bbox": [48.9826, 182.29074359999993, 546.5648398199997, 208.69268720000002], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "1 Department of Medicine, University Health Network, University of Toronto, Toronto, ON, Canada, 2 Division of Infectious Diseases and Tropical Medicine, Georgetown University Medical Center, Washington, DC, USA, 3 Queen Mary University of London, London, UK, 4 Thacker and Thompson, Atlanta, Georgia, USA, 5 MRL Research Laboratories, Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, New Jersey, USA, and 6 MRL Research Laboratories, MSD France, Puteaux, France"}, {"bbox": [48.9785, 221.09750000000008, 547.1689500000002, 241.56487757909224], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 5, "source": "docling", "text": "Background. Females and persons of Black race are often underrepresented in clinical trials. This post hoc analysis of data from three phase 3 studies evaluated the efficacy and safety of doravirine (DOR) by sex and race in adults living with HIV-1."}, {"bbox": [48.97849999999999, 245.07550000000015, 547.1746500000004, 301.5953775790923], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 6, "source": "docling", "text": "Methods. DRIVE-FORWARD and DRIVE-AHEAD open-label extensions were pooled; participants randomized to first-line DOR-based regimen continued from week (W) 96 to W192 (DOR-continued group) and participants randomized to comparators switched to DOR from W96 to W192 (DOR-switch group). In DRIVE-SHIFT, virologically suppressed adults were randomized to switch to a DOR-based regimen on day 1 (immediate-switch group) or W24 (delayed-switch group) and continued through W144. Results are reported by sex assigned at birth (male vs female) and race (Black vs non-Black)."}, {"bbox": [48.96899999999994, 304.9445000000002, 547.1642000000004, 373.5863775790923], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 7, "source": "docling", "text": "Results. Across trials, female and Black participants each represented < 20% of study populations. After continuing or switching to DOR, percentages of participants with HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL were comparable between sex and race subgroups. Mean changes in CD4+ T-cell counts and proportions of participants with drug-related adverse events or serious adverse events were generally  similar  between  subgroups.  In  DRIVE-SHIFT,  higher  rates  of  nontreatment-related  discontinuations  were  observed within Black versus non-Black subgroups. Differences in median weight change were generally larger between race subgroups than sex subgroups, although interquartile ranges were wide for all."}, {"bbox": [48.959499999999935, 377.04000000000013, 547.1357000000002, 409.5818775790923], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 8, "source": "docling", "text": "Conclusions. Participants who continued or switched to DOR generally had comparable efficacy and safety outcomes across sex and race subgroups. However, the sample size was limited. Future studies should ensure greater diversity when investigating factors leading to outcome disparities."}, {"bbox": [58.507, 413.0583, 313.57250000000005, 421.56517757909216], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 9, "source": "docling", "text": "ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT02275780, NCT02403674, NCT02397096."}, {"bbox": [58.507000000000005, 425.07579999999996, 416.1554, 433.5845775790922], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 10, "source": "docling", "text": "Keywords. DEI; diversity; human immunodeficiency virus; inclusion; participant selection."}, {"bbox": [48.9832, 452.40349999999995, 290.17395000000005, 577.8715775790921], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 11, "source": "docling", "text": "Demographic parameters, including sex assigned at birth, gender identification, age, race, or ethnicity, may have effects on treatment  efficacy  and  safety  that  cannot  be  predicted  when evaluating a new investigational drug [1-5]. To ensure equitable  access  to  health  advances  and  the  generalizability  of  research  findings,  many  investigators,  agencies,  and  advocacy groups have prioritized improved inclusivity of diverse populations in clinical trials to help identify any potential effects of demographic parameters on efficacy  or  tolerability  early  in  the clinical development process [6-9]."}, {"bbox": [56.0125, 603.5311448, 273.0461988599996, 610.5309448], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 12, "source": "docling", "text": "Received 10 December 2024; accepted 09 June 2025; published online 16 July 2025"}, {"bbox": [48.9852672, 611.1167436, 289.5557935599998, 628.5046887999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 13, "source": "docling", "text": "† K.S. was an employee of Merck Sharp & Dohme LLC, a subsidiary of Merck & Co., Inc., Rahway, NJ, USA, at the time the study was conducted."}, {"bbox": [48.9852672, 630.5206312, 289.5361941199997, 646.5361736], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 14, "source": "docling", "text": "Correspondence: Rima Lahoulou, MD, MRL Research Laboratories, MSD France, 10-12 Cours Michelet, 92800 Puteaux, France (rima.lahoulou@msd.com)."}, {"bbox": [48.9852672, 649.1007436, 147.08468440000001, 657.5328594], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 15, "source": "docling", "text": "Open Forum Infectious Diseases ®"}, {"bbox": [48.9826, 659.5431447999999, 289.54892647999964, 702.5499159999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 16, "source": "docling", "text": "© The Author(s) 2025. Published by Oxford University Press on behalf of Infectious Diseases Society  of  America.  This  is  an  Open  Access  article  distributed  under  the  terms  of  the Creative Commons Attribution License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), which permits unrestricted reuse, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited."}, {"bbox": [48.9826, 704.50986, 141.46395760000004, 711.5096599999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 17, "source": "docling", "text": "https://doi.org/10.1093/ofid/ofaf356"}, {"bbox": [306.0228, 452.40349999999995, 547.1756000000001, 711.8889775790922], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 1, "seq": 18, "source": "docling", "text": "Females and persons of Black race constitute the majority of those living with HIV worldwide; however, the response to the global HIV epidemic has historically been delayed and disparate in these populations, in which these individuals remain underrepresented in HIV antiretroviral clinical trials [1, 2]. As a consequence, pooling data from clinical trials has been necessary  to  evaluate  sufficient  numbers  in  these  demographics. For  example,  2  analyses  that  used  pooled  data  from  phase  3 clinical trials of integrase inhibitor-based regimens in participants living with HIV-1 (first-line and treatment experienced) demonstrated that response to antiretroviral therapy can vary by  sex  and  race  [1,  2].  The  proportion  of  participants  who achieved virologic suppression was numerically lower among participants who  were Black (vs non-Black) [2], female (vs  male)  [2],  and  Black  male  (vs  Black  female  or  non-Black male) [1]. The differences observed in these trials may be due to higher early discontinuation rates in these subgroups [1, 2]. These reports highlight that findings from clinical trials lacking in participant diversity may not be generalizable to all people living with HIV, as effectiveness and tolerability may not have been"}], "checksum": "17d0bad050affce6648ed8f491f5704aec9d9aad98dbd43bc733c8558a5460c5", "content_present": true, "doc_id": "d-410c06ede77fb6c4", "docling_version": "2.118.0", "engine_version": "2.118.0", "errors": [], "images": [{"bbox": [493.1352797209031, 12.63312295161586, 545.2407628003169, 55.08351606558699], "blob": "", "caption": "", "checksum": "9fe304bb887cb0502753be688d2a4f82067e1891b2911c2d97aa9f9e5a364b84", "mime": "image/png", "page": 1, "storage_ref": ""}, {"bbox": [348.57602741044354, 17.641401087504278, 481.290257345631, 49.213740170441724], "blob": "", "caption": "", "checksum": "92751651a5bd791df17d672c77ad220ea776ba216369f4ecfd4537560b234fe1", "mime": "image/png", "page": 1, "storage_ref": ""}], "page_index": 0, "page_sizes": {"1": [593.9719848632812, 782.9860229492188]}, "route": "docling", "schema_version": "v0.1.0", "source_hash": "410c06ede77fb6c4c9c3f72503815efe8ca1fa5bd31c9e508dfc860857eb38a2", "status": "ok", "tables": [], "timings": {}}